# vehje, known gaps

## no-std

The top-level vehje bin crate currently runs on std. The bin entry
point uses `std::env::args` and `std::process::exit`, both of which
have no stable no_std equivalent on stable Rust without target-
specific entry-point work (a custom `#[start]` shim or a libc-backed
main wrapper). This is the canonical ecosystem-fit case for std per
the no_std-first doctrine in `PRINCIPLES.md`. A future round
explores whether a `core::ffi::CStr`-based argv reader and a
libc-backed exit wrapper can replace the std entry, at which point
this gap closes and `#![no_std]` lands. Tracked under follow-up.
